"keykey.general.zhuyinLayoutHint" = "Where the 注音 symbols sit on the keyboard, effective immediately. Standard (大千) is the layout printed on Taiwanese keyboards and the one the original Yahoo! KeyKey shipped. Space is the first tone; 1–9 pick a candidate once the window is up. In 注音, associated phrases are always picked with Shift + a number — whatever the setting above says — because the number keys type 注音 there.";
"keykey.general.strokeConfirmation" = "Press Space to confirm the code";
"keykey.general.strokeConfirmationHint" = "In 速成, and in 倉頡 with the * wildcard, candidates appear before the code is finished, so Space flips to the next page instead of confirming what you typed. With this on, the first Space only confirms the code and keeps page 1 — press Space again to page, or 1–9 to pick. Plain 倉頡 is unaffected.";
"keykey.general.adaptiveCandidateOrder" = "Adapt candidate order based on your selections";
"keykey.general.adaptiveCandidateOrderHint" = "Applies to 倉頡, 速成, 注音 and associated phrases. Every candidate list is learned on its own: within a list, the candidates you have committed more often come first, and candidates you have committed equally often keep their built-in order. A 倉頡 code with a wildcard is learned separately from a complete code, and what is learned about 聯想字詞 is shared by 倉頡, 速成 and 注音. 拼音 keeps ranking candidates exactly as it did before. Turn it off for the built-in order — 五代 and 拼音 use their built-in rankings, 三代 and 注音 the original Yahoo! KeyKey order — which also pauses counting everywhere, without erasing what you have already learned.";
"keykey.general.language" = "Language";

/* What's New pane (2.15.0) */
"app.whatsNew.summary" = "注音 (ㄅ半) is back, and it works the way it always did: one syllable, one character. Type the 注音 symbols, finish the syllable with a tone (Space is the first tone), and the candidates appear — 1–9 picks. Start the next character and the one on screen is committed for you, so you never press Enter mid-sentence. Choose the 標準 (大千) or 倚天 keyboard. 倉頡, 速成 and 拼音 are untouched.";
"app.whatsNew.added1" = "The 注音 (ㄅ半) input method. Type the 注音 symbols and finish the syllable with a tone — Space is the first tone, as on any 注音 keyboard — and the candidate window opens: 1–9 picks, Space and the arrow keys page. Start the next character's first symbol and the one on screen is committed for you, so a sentence runs on without pressing Enter between characters. 聯想字詞 follows each commit, exactly as in 倉頡 and 速成. Candidates come from the original Yahoo! KeyKey ㄅ半 table in that table's own order (ㄍㄨㄛˊ → 國, ㄉㄜ˙ → 的), and what you pick is then learned for that reading alone. Add it in System Settings ▸ Keyboard: click Edit… beside Input Sources — the + is inside that sheet, not on the settings page — then + ▸ Chinese, Traditional ▸ 注音, and log out and back in as you would for any newly added input method.";
"app.whatsNew.added2" = "A choice of 注音 keyboard: 標準 (大千) or 倚天. 大千 is the default — the layout printed on Taiwanese keyboards, and the one the original Yahoo! KeyKey shipped. Switch it in 設定… ▸ 輸入方式, or straight from the input menu while 注音 is active; it applies to the next keystroke.";
"app.whatsNew.changed1" = "Two keys behave differently in 注音, because 注音 needs them. On 大千 the symbols ㄝ ㄡ ㄤ ㄥ ㄦ sit on , . ; / and -, so those keys type 注音 rather than punctuation, and ，。 move to Shift + , and Shift + . — where the original Yahoo! KeyKey put them. And because the number row types 注音 too, 聯想字詞 is always picked with Shift + a number in this mode, whatever 聯想選字鍵 is set to, which leaves a bare number free to type ㄅ ㄉ ㄓ ㄚ ㄞ ㄢ or a tone. Nothing changes for 倉頡, 速成 or 拼音.";

